<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">O Fortuna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;O Fortuna&quot; is a medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Goliardic poem of uncertain authorship, written in the early 13th century. It belongs to the collection known as the Carmina Burana, preserved in the Benediktbeuern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a>. The poem is a complaint against Fortuna, in Roman mythology the inexorable fate that rules both gods and mortals.</p></div>
